/7 CASSETTE ODT   (CODT)                  PAL8-V10D NO DATE   PAGE 14


             /CODT NORMALLY RUNS WITH DF=FLD BUT SOME ROUTINES
             /RUN WITH DF=F

             /THE STARTING LOCATION IS 'READ3', BUT YOU CAN START
             /AT LOCATION  'READ' IF YOU WANT TO RECOVER FROM A 'BOMB'

             /READ:  READS A COMMAND LINE
             /       RESTORES BP LOC IN CASE CODT WAS MANUALLY STARTED
             /       IF FIRST CHAR IS IN TABLE, BRANCH TO APPROPRIATE ROUTINE
             /       OTHERWISE ASSUMES DIGIT, GOES TO 'SEX'

             /SEX:   BALKS IF NOT NUMBER
             /       PUTS 4 DIGIT NUMBER IN 'WORD'
             /       EVENTUALLY FINDS A LETTER AND BRANCHES THRU DISPATCH TABLE

             /'/' SENDS YOU TO 'EXAM'

             /EXAM:  PUTS C(WORD) IN 'CAD'           **SLOPPY NOTATION**
             /       PRINTS C(CAD) IN FIELD F
             /       SIGNALS OPEN REGISTER
             /       GOES TO 'READ5'

             /CRL:   IF NUMBER PRECEEDED, USE IT TO MODIFY PREVIOUS
             /       LOCATION IF ONE WAS OPEN.
             /       RETURNS WITH DF=F

             /CR     SENDS TO CRL1

             /CRL1:  CALLS CRL
             /       THEN GOES TO 'READ'

             /LF SENDS TO CRL2

             /CRL2:  TYPE CR
             /       CALL CRL
             /       BUMP 'CAD'
             /       PRINT NEW CAD THEN /
